response:
Loops are used to repeatedly execute a block of code.  Here are two examples:

for (n = 0; n < 10; n++) {
    printNumber(n);
}

for (x = 0; x < 10; x++) {
    incrementVariable(x);
}

In both examples, the code to be executed is the same, but the loop will execute a fixed number of times, depending on the value of the loop variable.  The loop variable increments by 1 in the first example, and 10 in the second example.

